  === RISK FACTORS ===

  R1. REGIME LAG: Regime detection uses daily bars → up to 24h delay.
      Mitigation: Transition smoothing (blend over 12-24 bars).

  R2. OVERFITTING WEIGHTS: Empirical weights fit to historical regimes.
      Mitigation: Train/test split. Use conservative binary method as floor.
      Rule: Never allocate more than 2x the static baseline weight.

  R3. WHIPSAW COST: Rapid regime transitions cause position churn.
      Mitigation: Hysteresis — regime must persist N bars before switching.
      Minimum hold through regime transitions (don't force-exit).

  R4. REGIME DISTRIBUTION SHIFT: Post-ETF regime distribution differs.
      Mitigation: Use recent 3-month rolling weights as secondary signal.
      Weight table updated monthly from rolling performance.

  R5. WEIGHT NORMALIZATION: Dynamic weights may not sum to target.
      Mitigation: Normalize so sum(weights) = sum(base_weights) * budget_factor.
      Budget factor ∈ [0.5, 1.5] — never go below half or above 1.5x base.

